                                                                            <th>Brief Profile:</th>
                                                                            <td><p align="justify">Prof. Smita Chaturvedi is presently working as a Professor of Hindi Discipline in the School of Humanities at Indira Gandhi National Open University (IGNOU), New Delhi. She is a distinguished academician specializing in Premchand Hindi novels, folklores, and medieval poetry. With nearly three decades of dedicated teaching, she has significantly contributed to Hindi language and literature through various national and international platforms. Prof. Chaturvedi has edited several scholarly IGNOU course materials and played a key role in developing acclaimed IGNOU courses for Under graduate and PG programs including creative writing in Hindi, Hindi Sahitya Ka Itihas, Madhyakalin Kavita, Premchand, Writing for Radio and Hindi novels. Her extensive contributions include coordinating and advancing e-learning initiatives such as e-PG Pathshala and MOOCs (UGC). She has delivered lectures at various universities and institutions across India.</br> 
</br>
Apart from her recognition in the literary fraternity, she is the programme coordinator of MA Hindi (MHD) which was awarded the Best Programme Award on Foundation Day held on 19th November, 2024. She has given her contribution as a member in many prestigious committees like the  Executive Council, Academic Council, Board of Studies, School Board etc. at IGNOU and in many other Indian universities as well. She presented papers at the World Hindi Conferences. Prof. Chaturvedi also served as Visiting Professor at the ICCR Hindi Chair, Peking University, Beijing.Currently she is working as Director of School of Humanities, IGNOU New Delhi from 1st  October 2025.</p></td>
