                                                                            <th>Brief Profile:</th>
                                                                            <td><p>Jitendra Kumar Srivastava, hails from Deoria District in Uttar Pradesh. He completed his graduation from Gorakhpur and later studied for his Masters and Doctorate in Hindi Literature from JNU, New Delhi.</p><p>He is presently working as a Professor of Hindi Literature in the School of Humanities and also holding the post of Registrar, Administration Division since 6th November 2025.</p><p>He has also held the postitions of Registrar (Admin), Director, School of Tourism & Hospitality Service Management, and Director, International Division, IGNOU in the past. </p><p>He is a renowned poet and critic with 30 books to his credit, which include In Dino Halchal, Anbhay Katha, Asunder-Sunder, Bilkul Tumhari Tarah, Kayantaran, Bharatiya Samaj, Rashtravadaur Premchand, Sarjak Ka Swapn, Vichardhara, Naye Vimarshaur Samkaleen Kavita, Upanyaski Paridhi and Rachanaka Jeevdravya. His literary criticism has received world-wide recognition in the domain of Hindi literature. He has been admired by various social networking sites and his literary and academic contributions are deeply cited.</p><p>Apart from his recognition in the literary fraternity, he has received several prestigious awards that include the Bharat Bhushan Aggarwal Puraskar, Devishankar Awasthee Samman, Bhartiya Bhasha Parishad Puraskar, Ram Chandra Shukla Puraskar, Vijay Dev Narayan Sahi Puraskar, Kriti Samman, Ram Vilas Sharma Alochana Puraskar, Parampara RiturajSamman, Gopal Krishan Rath Samman, etc.</p><p>He has delivered more than 250 lectures at various universities and institutions across India. 14 Ph.D and one post-doctoral scholars have completed their research work under his supervision.  More than 10 research works have also been undertaken on his prominent literary works. Bhartiya Gyanpeeth has also published renowned books like Godaan, Rangbhumi and Dhruvswamini with the introductory note by Prof. Jitendra Srivastava. He has contributed more than 30 chapters in various edited books. He has also been a jury member of various important awards like the Bhartiya Gyanpeeth Navlekhan Puraskar etc.</p><p>He has given his contribution as a member in many prestigious committees like the Board of Management, Executive Council, Academic Council, Board of Studies, School Board etc. at IGNOU and in many other Indian universities as well. </p></td>
