                                                                        <tr>
                                                                            <th>Brief Profile:</th>
                                                                            <td><p>Dr. Shakir Ali Siddiqui is serving as an Assistant Professor in the Discipline of Urdu, School of Humanities, at Indira Gandhi National Open University (IGNOU), New Delhi. He obtained his Bachelor’s degree from Mumtaz P.G. College, University of Lucknow, his Master’s degree in Urdu from Aligarh Muslim University, and earned his M.Phil. and Ph.D. in Urdu from Jamia Millia Islamia, New Delhi.<br>
He served as a Senior Research Fellow at Jamia Millia Islamia for three years, during which he was actively engaged in teaching and research. Subsequently, he worked as an Assistant Professor in the Department of Urdu, Bhagwant University, Ajmer (Rajasthan) for nearly one and a half years, where he successfully supervised four M.Phil. dissertations on diverse literary topics. At present, Dr. Siddiqui is associated with IGNOU, where he not only teaches Urdu Language and Literature but also serves as the Coordinator for the Ph.D. Programme, M.A. (Applied Urdu), and several other courses. He is currently supervising four Ph.D. research scholars under his guidance.<br>
Dr. Siddiqui’s primary areas of research interest include poetry and literary criticism, with a particular focus on classical Urdu poetry and the principles of practical criticism. He takes keen interest in the analytical and aesthetic study of poetic texts, viewing literature not merely as an artistic experience but as a fusion of intellectual, creative, and cultural expression.<br>
He has authored dozens of research papers and book chapters on various aspects of Urdu criticism and poetry.
Recently, his book titled “Meer Anis ka Khusoosi Mutala” (Special Study of Mir Anis) was published and has been prescribed in the M.A. Urdu syllabus of the Directorate of Distance Education, University of Kashmir. Dr. Siddiqui’s scholarship is marked by wide reading, refined expression, and a balanced analytical approach. His academic and pedagogical pursuits are closely aligned with the mission of IGNOU, which seeks to make education accessible, equitable, and a means of holistic social advancement.</p></td>
